  "about": "A common-law couple in Alberta. One had two part-time jobs at once: each employer used the whole basic exemption, so less CPP was deducted than required and the credits use what was deducted (Schedule 8, Part 3b). The other, a student, earned less than the basic exemption and $2,000 of insurable earnings in a summer job: all the CPP and EI deducted comes back (lines 44800 and 45000). The first claims the couple's Canada workers benefit on Alberta's Schedule 6 (5009-S6): 21% of the $34,900 of family working income over $2,760, up to $2,619, not reduced since the adjusted family net income of $32,740 is under $32,772. Synthetic data.",
